{"type":"text","timestamp":1789791434939,"sessionID":"ses_f4824f550ffeaBmxcEcK2h5aW9","part":{"id":"prt_0b7e1ddef001UhKijl4HOGDMKW","messageID":"msg_0b7e1ca65001FcPOv5tsvMma60","sessionID":"ses_f4824f550ffeaBmxcEcK2h5aW9","type":"text","text":"Fixed the ownership regression with focused changes to four Lua source files.\n\n- **Job transitions:** `removeLock.lua` now validates the caller’s token before deleting the lock or changing stalled tracking. Stale completion, failure, immediate retry, and delayed retry use the existing lock-mismatch error.\n- **Lock renewal:** Single-job and batch renewal now require matching tokens, preventing stale workers from extending or replacing another owner’s lock.\n- **Retry side effects:** Delayed-job promotion now happens after ownership validation, so rejected retries leave events and queue state untouched.\n- Preserved missing-lock behavior and the administrative `\"0\"` token path.\n\nAdded six regression tests in `tests/worker-ownership.redis.test.ts`, covering recovery, rejected-operation invariants, renewal, current-owner completion, and administrative compatibility.\n\n**Verification on Node v24.21.0:**\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- Supplied seven-file regression command — **268 tests passed**.\n- New ownership regression suite — **6 tests passed**.\n\nNo existing tests, package files, build scripts, configuration, or dependencies were edited.","time":{"start":1789791428079,"end":1789791434938},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_02ee72d33ff75775016aae0cc3fab487d1ac02591339a455a8","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
